<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bay of Fundy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bay of Fundy is an inlet of the Atlantic between New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, with a small part touching Maine. It has the highest tidal range in the world, reaching about 16 metres. Its shores were the heart of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>, where settlers founded Port-Royal in 1605 and drained the tidal marshes with dykes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bay-of-fundy.jpg" alt="Bay of Fundy" width="300" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Decumanus at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wpdms_nasa_topo_bay_of_fundy_-_en.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
